# SECURITY BARRIER. This file is the only thing standing between the host's real
# secrets and PII and a published image layer. The Dockerfile's COPY list is
# deliberately narrow, so nothing below is load-bearing for the build -- it is
# load-bearing for the day someone "simplifies" that COPY into `COPY . .`.
#
# Rule of thumb used here: exclude by DIRECTORY, not by file extension, wherever
# the two could collide. `audio/` excludes recordings; a blanket `*.mp4` would
# also have deleted frontend/assets/avatar-talking.mp4, which is the thing the
# page actually loads.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets ----
# .env holds a real OPENROUTER_API_KEY, an HF_TOKEN and the live model choices.
# The whole family goes, not just `.env`: excluding one filename is a rule that
# survives until someone adds `.env.local` and nobody checks the new file. There
# is nothing in the image that reads any of them -- the values are injected at
# run time by compose's env_file, which reads the host file without ever putting
# it in a layer.
.env
.env.*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- PII ------
# Real personal data, never to leave the machine in an image:
#   wiki/       legal name, birth year, city, university, work history
#   candidate/  generated from wiki/, same content in Markdown
#   RAGraw/     the CV as a PDF
# These are bind-mounted read-only by docker-compose.yml instead.
wiki/
candidate/
RAGraw/

# Also exclude them under any nesting, in case one is ever moved without the
# root-level pattern being revisited.
**/wiki/
**/candidate/
**/RAGraw/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- app state -----
# Written at run time. audio/ has thousands of recorded answers on this host and
# must never be baked; data/ holds the SQLite conversation store (the most
# sensitive thing this project produces) and its *.db.bak-* backups.
audio/
data/
reports/
backend/.rag_cache/

# Belt and braces for a database that ends up somewhere else: every SQLite
# artifact, by extension, wherever it sits.
*.db
*.db.bak-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Recorded-media extensions, but NOT *.mp4/-- frontend/assets ships .mp4 avatars
# that the page needs, so this rule is narrower than it looks on purpose.
*.mp3
*.wav
*.webm
*.ogg

# ------------------------------------------------------- build inputs no ----
# None of these are read at run time. .venv/venv/python/build and
# interviewtts.egg-info would copy a WINDOWS virtualenv (already-resolved
# .exe launchers, wrong ABI) over the image's own site-packages. node_modules is
# the JS test runner's tree.
#
# Every directory pattern below is written `**/name/` rather than `name/`, and
# that is not style. Docker anchors a pattern CONTAINING a slash against the
# full path relative to the context root, so a bare `.ruff_cache/` matches
# `/.ruff_cache/` and nothing else -- it silently ignored
# `backend/.ruff_cache`, which is where this repository's actually keeps it.
# The first build shipped 5 __pycache__ directories and 2 .ruff_cache
# directories because of exactly that. `**/` is the only spelling that matches
# at every depth. (Patterns with NO slash at all, like `*.db`, already match a
# basename at any depth and need no prefix.)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.eggs/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/build/
**/dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
python/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# --------------------------------------------------------- not project code --
# Tooling, local indexes and working documents. `original/` is a nested git
# clone (a gitlink), `wikiDocs/` an Obsidian vault whose manifest references the
# private wiki, `.codegraph/` a derived index, `.atl/` and `.measure/` local
# runtime state.
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
.codegraph/
.atl/
.measure/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
openspec/
auditoria/
interviewtts-docs/
wikiDocs/
original/
nginx/
avatar/
"Nueva carpeta/"
scripts/
tests/
docs/

# Windows host litter, which would otherwise show up as unreadable-name noise
# in the build context.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
nul
*.lnk

# The Docker artefacts themselves, so a rebuild never sees the last one.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yaml
compose.yaml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- logs ------
*.log